Subject: [PATCH] fix(qwen): write Qwen Code 1.x its providers schema (#6867)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed: Qwen Code 1.x (v1.0.0-preview.1 on) reads the models of
the user's own from a top-level providers object, keys every model
provider/model — model.name among it — and resolves a provider's apiKey
from the environment, with no env object of its own in the settings;
0.x read modelProviders.openai and matched a bare entry id, so the
settings magpie wrote (0.x's schema, model.name a bare wire id) gave a
1.x qwen nothing to find and /model showed none of magpie's models.

magpie now writes a 1.x qwen providers.magpie — the catalog as
models[].model (displayName, contextWindow from 0.x's
generationConfig.contextWindowSize), apiKey a ${MAGPIE_QWEN_API_KEY}
reference whose key goes in ~/.qwen/.env, 1.x's schema having no env
object of its own — and model.name keyed magpie/<wire id>; the auth
type openai stays (1.x's provider-backed one). Which form to write is
the CLI's version (installedVersion, as fx asks fx's); a version
magpie cannot learn is taken for 1.x when the file has a providers
object (0.x's schema has none, and providers.magpie is magpie's own
wiring, which keeps a wired 1.x on 1.x when its CLI has left the
PATH), else for 0.x, as fx takes an unknown for an older fx. A 0.x
wiring of magpie's own left in a file a 1.x qwen now reads — its
entries in modelProviders.openai, the key in the env object, the
baseUrl beside model.name — goes whenever magpie next wires the file,
either way; the user's own entries stay. Stepping out takes only
magpie's back, 1.x's key from ~/.qwen/.env now too.

Run: go test -tags nogui -run 'TestQwen' ./internal/agent (0.x suite
pinned to 0.28.0, the 1.x suite to 1.0.0-preview.1, the unknown one to
""): ok. go vet -tags nogui ./internal/agent ./internal/cli on darwin,
linux and windows: clean. GOOS=each go build -tags nogui on the two
packages: ok. git diff --check: clean.

